tudy to assess human intestinal disaccharidases and hereditary disaccharide intolerance. It has also been used in a study to investigate the stimulation of sucrose degradation and starch synthesis in growing potato tubers.\nL197: ### Biochem/physiol Actions\nL198: \nL199: Palatinose is a disaccharide having an α(1→6) linkage between D-glucose and D-fructose and is similar to sucrose in its physicochemical properties. It is produced from sucrose in some bacteria by the action of sucrose isomerase. In mammalian gut, palatinose is hydrolyzed and absorbed much more slowly than sucrose.\nL200: ### Other Notes\nL201: \nL202: To gain a comprehensive understanding of our extensive range of 【15†Disaccharides】 for your research, we encourage you to visit our 【16†Carbohydrates】 Category page.\nL203: \nL204: * * *\nL205: \nL206: ## Compare Similar Items\nL207: \nL208: 【17†View Full Comparison】\nL209: \nL210: * * *\nL211: \nL212: Show Differences\nL213: \nL214: [Input]\nL215: \nL216: 1 of 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(±)-Potassium citramalate monohydrate ≥95.0% (NT) | Sigma-Aldrich (https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/aldrich/27455)\nciteturn116view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/aldrich/27455\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 383\nL0: 【0†Skip to Content】\nL1: \nL2: Products\nL3: \nL4: [Input]\nL5: \nL6: [Input: Type in Product Names, Product Numbers, or CAS Numbers to see suggestions.]\nL7: \nL8: Cart 0\nL9: \nL10: US EN\nL11: \nL12: Products\nL13: \nL14: [Input]\nL15: \nL16: [Input: Type in Product Names, Product Numbers, or CAS Numbers to see suggestions.]\nL17: \nL18: Products Applications Services Resources Support\nL19: \nL20: 【1†Login / Register】\nL21: \nL22: 【2†Order Lookup】\nL23: \nL24: 【3†Quick Order】\nL25: \nL26: Cart 0\nL27: \nL28: 【4†Products】\nL29: \nL30: 【5†Organic Building Blocks】\nL31: \nL32: 27455\nL33